#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:8
msgid "hugepages-control interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `hugepages-control` interface allows controlling [HugePages](https://"
"www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/vm/hugetlbpage.txt), a Linux kernel feature "
"that enables memory blocks to be managed in larger page sizes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:13
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:15
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:18
msgid ""
"This interface controls a resource shared by the whole system. Snaps that "
"use it can be installed as parallel instances, but every instance acts on "
"the same system resource and snapd does not coordinate between them. Make "
"sure each instance manages different resources, or run only one instance at "
"a time. See {ref}`Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-shared-resources>` for details.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:21
msgid "This interface assumes that _huge pages_ are mounted at either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:22
msgid "`/dev/hugepages` (Debian, Ubuntu)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:23
msgid "`/run/hugepages` (various other distributions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:25
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/hugepages-control-interface.md:27
msgid ""
